Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience equivalent to the STRL NM-04 Pay Band or equivalent GS Grade Level (GS-13/14) in the Federal Service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Examples of specialized experience for this position include: (1) Applying working knowledge and experience related to Professional Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Electronics Engineer, Aerospace Engineering and/or Computer Scientist concepts, processes and methodologies to function as a technical expert and consultant in areas relating to Electromagnetic Vulnerability, Lightning, Electromagnetic Pulse, Electrostatic Discharge, and P-Static simulation for assigned air weapons systems;
2) Demonstrating working knowledge and experience of major air weapons system design, testing, modeling, and simulation;
(3) Participating in approval of IT proposals, preparation of cost estimates, allocation of resources, financial oversight, problem resolution and final reporting in support agency mission and program objectives;
(4) Conducting operational analysis and formulation of air weapons system concepts, designs, functional specifications, and systems integration to meet the needs of new and emerging test requirements;
(5) Coordinating and/or assigning work assignments to subordinates, based on organizational priorities, selective consideration of difficulty and requirements of assignments, and/or capabilities of employees; and
(6) Providing project/program management to meet cost, schedule, and performance requirements for an aviation program. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management website:
