Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of Specialized experience at or equivalent to the GS-10 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following: 1) Maintaining and operating of mechanical distribution systems & equipment, and electrical distribution systems & equipment up to 69KV; 2) Applying, analytical and diagnostic techniques to these utility distribution systems, high and low voltage electrical and mechanical utility distribution safety practices and procedures; 3) Reading and understanding engineering drawings, sketches, specifications, material lists, and job/task orders. Understanding and use of electrical one lines and other utility system drawings. Understanding of utility monitoring systems such as Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition (SCADA) or equivalent; 4) Interpreting, troubleshooting and disseminating information concerning alarms and warnings, engineering graphics, computer aided design (CAD), and geographic information systems (GIS), Microsoft Office software including Access, Excel, Word; and 5) Communicating clearly and effectively - both orally and in writing - in order to formulate and present findings, briefings, narrative reports, and production summaries / metrics. Skilled in good customer relations. To be considered for GS-10:
